# Code owners — review routing by domain.
#
# Last matching pattern wins (GitHub semantics), so more specific paths are
# listed AFTER the general ones. Enabling "require review from Code Owners" is a
# maintainer setting (see the RFC checklist, Discussion #1087).
#
# SCALING NOTE. Today every domain resolves to the maintainer, so the file is
# valid and works immediately. As the project grows, create per-domain reviewer
# teams under the org and swap the owner on each domain's lines, e.g.:
#     lang      -> @zaplang-io/lang-reviewers
#     stdlib    -> @zaplang-io/stdlib-reviewers
#     runtime   -> @zaplang-io/runtime-reviewers
#     tooling   -> @zaplang-io/tooling-reviewers
# The path grouping below is already sharded by domain, so that swap is a
# one-owner-per-section edit. Do NOT reference a team that does not exist yet —
# an unknown owner is inert and can leave a required-review rule unsatisfiable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Global fallback.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @parveshgarg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Language: surface, type system, grammar, front/middle-end.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
